     "nodeId": "p3-drawing-root",
     "replacement": "**Feature**\t**Definition**\t**Example(s)**\n**Circumference**\tThe circumference of a circle is the perimeter, or distance around the outside of a circle.\t\n**Arc**\tAn arc is a continuous part of the circumference.\t\t\n**Centre**\tThe centre is the fixed point that is the same distance from every point on the circumference. A circle is the set of all points an equal distance from the centre.\t\n**Tangent**\tA tangent is a straight line that touches the circumference at a single point without entering the circle.\t\t\n**Chord**\tA chord is a straight line segment that goes from one point on the circumference to another point.\t\t",
     "autoApply": true,
